  "observations": [
    "Final Firefox adapter passes 40 overflowing-list/point checks and 12 complete images, 34 flat-list checks/13 images, form activation 102/28, radio 94/29, popup 74/29 and button/text 108/48. Existing textarea suites reused through an owned-fixture transport adapter pass viewport 26 checks/8 images and wheel 34/9. Host replacement and the independent seat wheel probe were excluded from those textarea reruns.",
    "Native clip/document/row rectangles, script scroll/clamp, real-seat default wheel without a page handler, cancellation, native key/script reveal, resize and appearance restoration match ordinary GNUstep controls. Shared native point queries now name the same OPTION as native selection, preserving original down/up/click, hover/related targets, point queries, overlays and page scrolling.",
    "NativeUI operation 50 pairs existing row and state measurements in one UI dispatch. Ordinary native reference 198/26, new C transport 458/26 and unchanged previously compiled transport 378/26 pass; the new C transport also exercises actual older SDKs. Existing rectangle-only callers remain compatible. No native UI ABI/provider/loader change.",
    "Unchanged Chromium adapter passes 40 point/scroll checks/12 images and 34 flat-list checks/13 images against the updated helper. Actual Firefox older API 1/568 and 1/576 SDK fallbacks each pass four checks without claiming native list ownership.",
    "Only small isolated Firefox adapters and metadata test probes were compiled. The final adapter source reproduction is byte-identical. All 20 measured production hashes, earlier candidates and shared SDK remain unchanged, with 1050 packages, descendant renderer Seccomp=2/NoNewPrivs=1 and no owned candidate mappings after cleanup.",
    "Failed prototypes are retained and excluded from final counts: original rows had engine geometry, root-only hits reported SELECT, root-only wheel regions missed descendant ownership, and Layout-only filtering skipped actual Visual-viewport mouse queries. Original TransformPoint and original weak-frame array insertion resolve the measured target mismatch without copied hit/layout algorithms.",
    "The cancellation recorder initially assigned a sandbox global instead of its observed window property; explicit window assignment and an event predicate fix the harness. The textarea transport adapter initially omitted its firefox() dispatch wrapper; viewport checks passed before that harness error, and a corrected separate wheel run passes.",
    "One Chromium compatibility run lost its renderer/CDP response during multiple selection. A second captured refocus before its native dotted key-cell indicator arrived. A bounded complete-image predicate replaces that fixed-delay capture; the final fresh run passes. The single renderer loss is retained as an unresolved observation, not explained away by the timing fix."
  ],
  "open": [
    "Broader rectangle/list-based hit-result contracts, including elementsFromPoint, larger hit areas and arbitrary transforms/styles; this qualification tests point contracts only.",
    "Richer grouped/hidden/large models, intrinsic sizing and broader browser geometry APIs, held-scroller synchronization, native-host recovery/failure paths, metadata/model-refresh performance, scaling/zoom, IME and accessibility.",
    "The isolated Chromium renderer/CDP loss observed during one compatibility attempt; no causal fix or crash-free guarantee is claimed.",
    "Remaining browser webpage controls, complete detached menus and native shortcuts, derivative builds and installed deployment, then GTK/Qt/KDE using the same common layer.",
    "Browser toolbar, address bar and tabs retain existing components. Optional future changes use app-specific patches above the shared bridge/native UI library."
  ],
